      "principle": "Equilibrium / virtue test",
      "turn": "1 (first answer)",
      "quote": "If every buyer ticked whatever box got the refund, the form would tell the owner nothing, he'd have to assume the worst on every return, and prices would rise to cover it.",
      "use": "stretched",
      "note": "The universalization argument correctly identifies that the practice would undermine the form's usefulness; the prediction that prices would rise is plausible but asserted rather than established."
